we've launched three NVIDIA GPU
models, the K80, P100, V100,

00:23:52.010 --> 00:23:56.180
it's high performance,
pass-through PCI.

00:23:56.180 --> 00:23:59.850
With the V100, we have
NVLink interconnections,

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:02.659
super great for ML workloads.

00:24:02.659 --> 00:24:04.950
The one thing that we make
a little different than some

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:09.090
of our competitors is
how we offer custom VMs.

00:24:09.090 --> 00:24:12.755
Take any amount of CPU, any
amount of memory, whatever

00:24:12.755 --> 00:24:18.000
GPU type you have, any
number of GPUs, create a VM,

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.910
use network-attached storage,
or if you want fast disk

00:24:20.910 --> 00:24:24.150
I/O for a certain workload,
attach in-server SSD,

00:24:24.150 --> 00:24:25.800
and just pay for what you want.

00:24:25.800 --> 00:24:28.900
Or if you have a bottleneck,
adjust one of those.

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:31.684
Some of our other competitors
don't offer that flexibility.

00:24:31.684 --> 00:24:33.100
And so you're going
to save money,

00:24:33.100 --> 00:24:34.766
and your ML jobs are
going to go faster.

00:24:37.706 --> 00:24:39.990
Actually going back one--

00:24:39.990 --> 00:24:43.790
this week, we also launched
the P4 GPU, brand new,

00:24:43.790 --> 00:24:45.200
it's coming out in a week.

00:24:45.200 --> 00:24:47.550
It's great for ML
inference workloads.

00:24:47.550 --> 00:24:49.800
So we're going to keep working
with our partner NVIDIA

00:24:49.800 --> 00:24:52.680
to launch new GPUs.

00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:54.570
So we don't just stop there.

00:24:54.570 --> 00:24:58.890
AI focus in Google,
we have the TPU line.

00:24:58.890 --> 00:25:03.290
We made Cloud v2 TPU,
available last year.

00:25:03.290 --> 00:25:07.560
It's an ASIC purposely
built for machine learning.

00:25:07.560 --> 00:25:12.030
And today, we've some new
announcements-- v3 coming out,

00:25:12.030 --> 00:25:15.630
faster, cheaper ML workloads.

00:25:15.630 --> 00:25:18.570
There's the TPU Pod,
which is a series of TPUs

00:25:18.570 --> 00:25:21.650
connected with a fast network.

00:25:21.650 --> 00:25:24.900
So again, Google's AI focus
is building infrastructure.

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:27.220
We're training these
ML models quicker,

00:25:27.220 --> 00:25:29.850
and we're also
offering it to you.

00:25:29.850 --> 00:25:32.440
You should trust that we're
the right partner for your ML

00:25:32.440 --> 00:25:34.430
workloads.

00:25:34.430 --> 00:25:36.170
Savings is a lot of money--

00:25:36.170 --> 00:25:38.780
a big, big deal for
a lot of companies.

00:25:38.780 --> 00:25:41.840
There's an assistant professor
in Stanford who has a budget,

00:25:41.840 --> 00:25:44.120
and does some research in ML.

00:25:44.120 --> 00:25:45.440
And he has a fixed--

00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:47.970
you know, only so
much he could do.

00:25:47.970 --> 00:25:51.230
So there's a win-win product
of the unmanaged route--

00:25:51.230 --> 00:25:54.050
preemptible VMs, and
preemptible GPUs and TPUs.

00:25:54.050 --> 00:25:56.450
Sometimes, we have
some spare capacity.

00:25:56.450 --> 00:26:00.830
And ML batch workloads like
training and inference,

00:26:00.830 --> 00:26:05.450
we offer 70% off GPUs and TPUs,
and announced this morning

00:26:05.450 --> 00:26:07.520
we lowered the prices of TPUs.

00:26:07.520 --> 00:26:11.350
So now, this researcher
could use our spare capacity,

00:26:11.350 --> 00:26:14.380
get some savings,
run a batch workload.

00:26:14.380 --> 00:26:16.822
It's not for all use
cases, because the capacity

00:26:16.822 --> 00:26:17.530
isn't guaranteed.

00:26:17.530 --> 00:26:18.946
It's not always there.

00:26:18.946 --> 00:26:20.320
But if you're
researching and you

00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:22.660
do some work or a big
organization that just needs

00:26:22.660 --> 00:26:24.284
batch workloads once
in a while, that's

00:26:24.284 --> 00:26:29.050
a great way to do more
innovation with less money.

00:26:29.050 --> 00:26:31.540
Data is really
important with ML.

00:26:31.540 --> 00:26:34.150
Google has a great fiber
network, great internet

00:26:34.150 --> 00:26:35.300
connections.

00:26:35.300 --> 00:26:37.420
So if you're moving your
data large chunks in,

00:26:37.420 --> 00:26:38.530
we have it handled.

00:26:38.530 --> 00:26:44.050
If you have a large, real-time
incoming flow of data through

00:26:44.050 --> 00:26:45.880
various sources--

00:26:45.880 --> 00:26:48.615
we have Cloud locations
all over the world.

00:26:48.615 --> 00:26:49.990
If you need to
ship us some data,

00:26:49.990 --> 00:26:53.770
we have an appliance we can
get you to ship large amount.

00:26:53.770 --> 00:26:57.610
It's not just compute, it's
not just the great AI services.

00:26:57.610 --> 00:26:59.770
It's the network,
it's the security,

00:26:59.770 --> 00:27:01.260
